<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Perfeddwlad</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Berfeddwlad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Perfeddwlad, the &quot;Middle Country&quot;, was the name for the four cantrefi of north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-conwy">River Conwy</a> and the River Dee: Rhos, Rhufoniog, Dyffryn Clwyd and Tegeingl. Lying between Gwynedd and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, it was repeatedly fought over by Welsh princes and English kings in the 12th and 13th centuries. After the conquest of 1283 it was divided between marcher lordships and the new county of Flint.</p></div>
